      "writtenOn": "2018-09-12T07:22:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I question whether it\u0027s actually appropriate to remove it. I understand it\u0027s not needed, but is it costly ? Or in better terms : are either of the following statements true ?\n- It\u0027s expensive to pass this argument [e.g. because it gets marshalled]\n- It\u0027s undesirable to pass this argument [e.g. because synchronous methods on the IpServer instance should not be called in the callback]\n\nIf neither, then my experience is that it\u0027s a lot easier to use if you do pass this argument. Sure, you could, say, embark it when you create your instance of a Callback, but having it passed relieves the implementor from that responsibility.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 124,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 124,
        "endChar": 56
      },
      "revId": "2df037e5116c180d9257d6b17bf9f6b8c24f88e7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d89de5e3_a3c49dba",
